What is an AI Model?

An AI Model (Artificial Intelligence Model) is a computer program that learns patterns from data and uses those patterns to make predictions, generate content, answer questions, classify information, or automate tasks.

An AI model is a trained software system that learns patterns from data and uses that knowledge to make predictions, generate content, or solve problems.

Think of it like this:

Data = Study Material
Training Process = Learning
AI Model = The trained student
Prediction/Response = The answer given by the student



Simple Example

If you show thousands of cat pictures to an AI model during training:

It learns the features of cats (ears, eyes, fur, shape).
Later, when you show a new image, it can identify whether it contains a cat or not.



